\title{Typography & basic styling}
\import{base-macros}
\tag{feature-demo}
\meta{style:tbl-sl2zcz}{align=center width=59}

\p{
  Body text supports \em{emphasis}, \strong{bold}, \dem{strong emphasis}, and
  \mark{highlight}. Inline code like \code{map f xs} sits in a beveled box, and
  inline math #{e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0} flows naturally with the surrounding prose.
}

\p{
  An \strong{unordered} list, with nesting and inline math:
}
\ul{
  \li{
    A first item with \em{emphasis}.
  }
  \li{
    A second item containing math: #{\sum_{k=1}^{n} k = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}}.
  }
  \li{
    A nested list:
    \ul{
      \li{
        nested item a
      }
      \li{
        nested item b
      }
    }
  }
}

\p{
  An \strong{ordered} list:
}
\ol{
  \li{
    First, establish the base case.
  }
  \li{
    Then, assume the inductive hypothesis.
  }
  \li{
    Finally, prove the inductive step.
  }
}

\blockquote{
  A block quotation is set apart from the body text — useful for definitions,
  remarks, or quoted passages.
}

\p{
  A horizontal rule separates sections:
}
\hr

\p{
  And a small table built from the \code{table} / \code{tr} / \code{th} /
  \code{td} macros:
}
\table{
  \tr{\th{Symbol}\th{Set}\th{Countable}}
  \tr{\td{#{\N}}\td{natural numbers}\td{yes}}
  \tr{\td{#{\Z}}\td{integers}\td{yes}}
  \tr{\td{#{\Q}}\td{rationals}\td{yes}}
  \tr{\td{#{\R}}\td{real numbers}\td{no}}
}

\p{
  Tables and image figures are centered at a sensible width by default. In the
  local dev server, hovering one brings up a small toolbar (align left / center /
  right, a width field) plus drag handles a right edge to resize, and per-column
  edges on tables; the chosen sizing is saved as a \code{\startverb\meta{style:…}\stopverb}
  line in the tree's frontmatter, leaving the table/figure markup untouched.
}
